    {
        "content": "<p>Interesting , although keep in mind the answer here isn’t actually ‘h’ , when you match on an and b in the body of the statement, since they are in a sort of dependent position in h, you are also matching on h.</p>\n<p>Just clarifying , don’t think there should be an error like that though.</p>\n<p>But I am not even sure it’s provable or inhabitable otherwise , if you try include the other patterns for example you will see there is a sort of recursion happening where no matter how many patterns you add it will ask for another.</p>\n<p>Yea I think the reason may be linked to this, because the goal of the proof is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x_1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But h itself is </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So then it does it again, and again and again and so on.</p>",
